if you have small cell lung cancer it is  often staged using a simpler two-part  system because treatment options don't  vary much between the more detailed  stages used to describe non-small-cell  lung cancer  in limited stage small cell lung cancer  cancer cells are found in one lung and  may be found in the tissues between the  lungs and in nearby lymph nodes if  cancer is found in the other lung in the  lymph nodes on the other side of the  chest or in other parts of the body it  is called extensive stage
 

